<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 5 September, from 1698 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1698">1698 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">328 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter the Great shaves his nobles' beards</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Back from his Grand Embassy to western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, Peter I personally cut off the beards of leading boyars. A tax on beards followed, part of his drive to westernise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s elite.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1774">1774 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">252 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Continental Congress meets in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from twelve colonies gathered at Carpenters' Hall to coordinate resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intolerable-acts">Intolerable Acts</a>. They agreed a boycott of British goods and planned to meet again.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1877">1877 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">149 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crazy Horse is killed at Camp Robinson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Oglala Lakota leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse">Crazy Horse</a>, a victor at Little Bighorn, was bayoneted by a soldier while resisting arrest at Camp Robinson, Nebraska. He died that night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Palestinian gunmen seize Israeli athletes at the Munich Olympics</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-september">Black September</a> militants killed two members of the Israeli team and took nine hostage. All nine and a West German policeman died in a failed rescue at Fürstenfeldbruck airbase.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lynette Fromme tries to shoot President Ford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manson Family follower Lynette 'Squeaky' Fromme aimed a pistol at Gerald Ford in Sacramento, but no round was chambered. A second attempt on Ford came 17 days later.</p></div></li></ol>
